      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِسَآءٌ مُؤَرْنَبٌ</span></b>  <i>A</i> [<i>garment of the kind called</i>]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كساء</span> <i>of which the thread is intermixed with the
soft hair of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْنَب</span> [or <i>hare</i>]; (T, S, M, K;)
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرْنَبٌ</span></b> , (so in a copy of the M,) or
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْنَبٌ</span></b> , like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَقْعَدٌ</span>: (A, K:) or, as some say, <i>i. q.</i>
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْنَبَانِىٌّ</span></b> . (T.) ― 
